  "api": "discoveryengine.v1",
  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Breaking Change: Many Fields Now Read-Only; New Feature Controls",
  "summary": "This update introduces several breaking changes where numerous API properties have been made read-only. Developers must update their code if they were previously writing to these fields. Additionally, new capabilities for managing feature toggles, provisioning project experiences, and custom OAuth scopes are now available.",
  "details": "A significant breaking change has been introduced: many properties across various schemas are now explicitly `readOnly`. If your integration previously wrote to fields such as `toolDisplayNames` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswer`, `delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed` or `effectiveFeatures` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine`, `experienceState` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Project`, or any of the feature toggle related fields within `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiSettings` and its sub-schemas, your code will now fail. These fields are now server-managed or output-only, providing internal state information rather than configurable parameters.\n\nOn the new features front, developers gain more granular control and visibility. `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ActionConfig` now supports `customerManagedScopes`, allowing you to specify custom OAuth scopes for connectors. The `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine` schema includes a new `globalFeatureToggleState` property, enabling control over the global rollout timing of features (e.g., `DELAYED`, `SCHEDULED`, `GENERAL`, `EARLY`). For project provisioning, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ProvisionProjectRequest` now accepts a `provisionIntent` to specify whether provisioning is for the new Gemini Enterprise experience (`PROVISION_INTENT_SOBI`) or the classic one (`PROVISION_INTENT_LEGACY`). Furthermore, the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DynamicTool` schema gains a `readonly` boolean property to indicate if a tool performs write operations. Finally, new output-only fields like `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine.effectiveFeatures` and the detailed `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfo` schemas provide enhanced visibility into the resolved state and launch stages of various features.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "Breaking Change",
    "Feature Management",
    "Provisioning",
    "Security",
    "Tools"
  ],
